Article 30
(1) Regional Government as referred to in Article 29 letter a, has the obligation and responsibility to:
a. respect, protect and fulfill the rights of victims and the special rights of child victims of violence;
b. formulate and implement programs and activities related to the protection of women and children;
c. implement protection of women and children from violence; d. supervise services for victims of violence based on minimum service standards in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
e. allocate budget for protection of women and children from violence according to regional financial capacity and budgeted in each fiscal year; and
f. realize Child-Friendly Regency.
(2) In order to formulate and implement effective women and children protection programs as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b, the Regional Government shall organize:
a. disaggregated gender and child data system; and
b. gender-responsive and child-friendly planning and budgeting. (3) Regional Government may establish Regional Technical Implementation Unit for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to reach services in the Region.

Part Four
Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children at the Sub-District Level Article 48 (1) The Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children at the Sub-District Level as referred to in Article 45 letter c, constitutes a functional work unit that organizes integrated protection services and handling of cases of violence against children and women at the Sub-District level.
(2) The Management of the Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children at the Sub-District Level as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of:
a. elements of the Sub-District apparatus;
b. agencies or institutions at the Sub-District level;
c. elements of the Sector Police;
d. elements of the Military District Command;
e. community leaders or religious leaders;
f. youth elements; and
g. elements of the Sub-District Family Welfare Development Mobilization Team. (3) The main duties of the Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children at the Sub-District Level as referred to in paragraph (1) are:
a. providing services in the context of protection of women and children;
b. receiving public complaints regarding cases of violence against women and children in the Sub-District and Village areas;
c. facilitating women and children who are victims of violence in resolving their problems;
d. socializing to the community about the protection of women and children; and
e. providing assistance for victims or referring to P2TP2A, sector police/resort police, hospitals or other institutions as required.
(4) Further provisions regarding the establishment, duties, and functions of the task force for the protection of women and children at the sub-district level as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be stipulated by Decree of the Sub-District Head.

Article 35
(1) Prevention as referred to in Article 34 letter a, shall be implemented by means of:
a. establishing a network in efforts to prevent violence; b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. establishing a violence prevention system;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children; and
e. providing knowledge about prevention and mechanisms for handling violence against women and children.
(2) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in an integrated manner by Regional Apparatus of the Regency and related agencies that have principal tasks and functions in the administration of affairs of: a. women's empowerment and child protection;
b. education;
c. health;
d. social affairs;
e. manpower;
f. youth and sports; and
g. mental and spiritual.
(3) In addition to being implemented by Regional Apparatus of the Regency and related agencies as referred to in paragraph (2), prevention shall also be implemented by: a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community, NGOs, community organizations, social organizations and religious organizations; and
c. business sector.

Article 29
Obligations and responsibilities in the implementation of protection for women and children are the shared responsibility of:
a. Regional Government;
b. village government;
c. Community; and
d. parents, Guardians and/or Family.

